<title>SINGAPORE: Indonesia allocates 225,000 bpd crude in Jan.</title>
<headline>Indonesia allocates 225,000 bpd crude in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia reduced its allocations of crude for export in January to 225,000 barrels per day (bpd) from 233,000 bpd in December, industry sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>They said the allocation of the key Minas grade was raised to 72,000 bpd from 69,000 bpd.</p>
<p>But key China favorites, Cinta and Widuri, were cut.</p>
<p>Cinta was reduced to 20,000 bpd from 24,000 bpd, while Widuri was cut to 11,000 bpd from 30,000 bpd.</p>
<p>The following allocations of key grades were made, industry sources said (in barrels per day);  </p>
<p>		   JAN	 DEC</p>
<p> MINAS	   72,000    69,000</p>
<p> DURI	    35,000    30,000</p>
<p> BONTANG MIX   32,000    30,000</p>
<p> CINTA	   20,000    24,000</p>
<p> BELIDA	  12,000    12,000</p>
<p> WIDURI	  11,000    30,000</p>
<p> ARUN	    19,000    22,000</p>
<p> TOTAL	  225,000   233,000</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3081)</p>
</text>
